## 1. Executive summary

| KPI | Value | Definition |
|---|---|---|
| **GMV** | ₹66.95 M | Sum of `basket_value` for delivered, valid-basket orders |
| **Orders** | 99,094 | Count of orders where `is_gmv_order = 1` |
| **Avg Delivery Min** | 24.0 min | Average of `delivery_minutes_clean` |
| **Churn Rate** | 8.8% | Share of customers flagged `churned_next_60d` |
| **Repeat Customer Rate** | 98.2% | Buyers with 2+ GMV orders ÷ all buyers (3,878 of 3,948) |
| Avg order value (derived) | ₹675.6 | GMV ÷ Orders (not shown on the dashboard) |

**Headline findings**

- **Strong growth.** Monthly GMV rose from ₹0.42 M (Jul 2025) to ₹9.89 M (Jun 2026), and monthly orders from 623 to 14,705. Growth is slowing: Jun 2026 was only +1.4% on May, after +8–27% month-on-month earlier in the series.
- **Bengaluru is the largest market** at ₹18.7 M (28% of GMV) and also the slowest for delivery (26.3 min). Jaipur is the smallest (₹7.3 M) with fast delivery (22.7 min).
- **Delivery time is driven by two factors:** peak hours (08–09 and 19–21 run about 27 min versus about 23 min otherwise) and rain (30.1 min versus 23.7 min).
- **Churn is concentrated** in `paid_social` customers (13.2%), free-plan users (10.0%) and dormant accounts (54.8%). Premium users churn at only 3.2%.

