### 2.2 Relationships

```
dim_city (1) ──< customers_clean (many)   on city          [active, single direction]
customers_clean (1) ──< orders_clean (many)   on customer_id [active, single direction]
```

This is a snowflake-style chain: `dim_city → customers_clean → orders_clean`. City slicers and city columns therefore filter orders **through the customer's city**. I checked the data: the customer's city matches `orders_clean.city` for every order, so results are consistent today.

